NPC: coroners_assistant_morgue
LOCATION: morgue
SCHEDULE: morning=morgue, midday=morgue, evening=morgue, night=closed

# Plain coat defaults: private observations, confidential medical notes, mutual trust
TOPIC: default
  GATE: coat = plain
  TAG: assistant_repeat_plain_notes
  WEIGHT: 3
  [The assistant sets down a pair of nickel-plated forceps, drying her fingers on a towel.]
  VOICE: violin_neutral_medium_v1
  THE CORONER'S ASSISTANT: "I speak more freely when the brass isn't reflecting off the tile, Walter. What I see under these lamps stays between our notebooks."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: coat = plain
  TAG: assistant_repeat_plain_formalin
  WEIGHT: 2
  VOICE: violin_weary_short_v1
  THE CORONER'S ASSISTANT: "The formalin smell gets into wool. You'll want to hang that coat by the stove tonight."

# Police coat / badge defaults: official records, Odell's vouchers, administrative detachment
TOPIC: default
  GATE: coat != plain
  TAG: assistant_repeat_badge_vouchers
  WEIGHT: 3
  [She points the tip of a scalpel toward the clipboard on the wall.]
  VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_medium_v2
  THE CORONER'S ASSISTANT: "If Captain Odell wants the certified autopsy transcripts, Officer, he must sign the morgue requisition slip."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: coat != plain
  TAG: assistant_repeat_badge_slabs
  WEIGHT: 2
  VOICE: violin_dismissive_short_v1
  THE CORONER'S ASSISTANT: "Official business only down here, Corwin. The coroner does not care for patrolmen idling beside the cold tables."

TOPIC: day_two_table
  GATE: day >= 2 AND NOT topic_done(coroners_assistant_morgue, day_two_table)
  TAG: assistant_day_two
  LABEL: "Return to the morgue"
  TIME: 5
  [Six of the eight tables now have county tags on their cards. Two do not.]
  VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_medium_v2
  THE CORONER'S ASSISTANT: "The captain's office sent a memorandum this morning.\nI'm to finalize the six identified decedents and hold the remaining two for registrar disposition."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Registrar disposition."
  VOICE: violin_neutral_short_v2
  THE CORONER'S ASSISTANT: "That is the language of the memorandum."
  WALTER CORWIN: "What does it mean in practice?"
  VOICE: violin_neutral_medium_v1
  THE CORONER'S ASSISTANT: "In practice it means I do not write cause of death on those two cards until I'm told I may."
  [She turns back to the preparation table. Her hands are very still.]
  VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_long_v2
  THE CORONER'S ASSISTANT: "I will tell you that there was no water in the woman's lungs.\nI will tell you that as a professional observation I am recording in my own notes, not the county file."
  NOTEBOOK: assistant_day_two | "The coroner's assistant is barred from filing cause of death for Naomi and the boy pending registrar disposition. She recorded independently that there was no water in Naomi's lungs — not drowning."
  EVIDENCE: no_water_lungs

TOPIC: day_three_table
  GATE: day >= 3 AND evidence(no_water_lungs) AND NOT topic_done(coroners_assistant_morgue, day_three_table)
  TAG: assistant_day_three
  LABEL: "Ask what the registrar's disposition found"
  TIME: 4
  [The two untagged tables are empty. The sheets are folded on the chairs beside them.]
  WALTER CORWIN: "The two from beyond the birches."
  VOICE: violin_neutral_short_v2
  THE CORONER'S ASSISTANT: "Removed yesterday evening. Registrar's order."
  WALTER CORWIN: "To where?"
  VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_medium_v2
  THE CORONER'S ASSISTANT: "The order did not specify.\nI asked. I was told the county would handle the arrangement."
  [She folds a piece of lint cloth twice, precisely, and sets it in a drawer.]
  VOICE: violin_neutral_medium_v1
  THE CORONER'S ASSISTANT: "I kept my notes.\nIf anyone asks me under oath what I observed, I will say exactly what I observed.\nI hope someone asks."
  NOTEBOOK: assistant_day_three | "Naomi and the boy were removed from the morgue on a registrar's order with no stated destination. The assistant kept her private notes and stated she will testify if asked."
